[774] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m```[39m                                                               [0m]8;;
[775] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[776] (w=67)  That gives you a popup searchable list of agent panes.            [0m]8;;
[777] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[778] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[39m [0m]8;;
[779] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[780] (w=67)  [38;2;255;158;100m[1mImportant caveat[22m[39m                                                  [0m]8;;
[781] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[782] (w=67)  This works best if [38;2;158;206;106m#{pane_current_command}[39m actually shows the     [0m]8;;
[783] (w=67)  agent name.                                                       [0m]8;;
[784] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[785] (w=67)  Usually that’s true when the agent is the foreground process. But [0m]8;;
[786] (w=67)  sometimes you may just see:                                       [0m]8;;
[787] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[788] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[38;2;158;206;106mbash[39m                                                            [0m]8;;
[789] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[38;2;158;206;106mzsh[39m                                                             [0m]8;;
[790] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[38;2;158;206;106mfish[39m                                                            [0m]8;;
[791] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[792] (w=67)  instead of [38;2;158;206;106mpi[39m/[38;2;158;206;106mcodex[39m, depending on how it’s launched.              [0m]8;;
[793] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[794] (w=67)  [38;2;255;158;100m[1mIf that happens[22m[39m                                                   [0m]8;;
[795] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[796] (w=67)  You still have two good options.                                  [0m]8;;
[797] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[798] (w=67)  [38;2;255;158;100m[1m### [22m[39m[38;2;255;158;100m[1mOption 1: launch agents via wrapper[22m[39m                           [0m]8;;
[799] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[800] (w=67)  When starting an agent, set pane metadata:                        [0m]8;;
[801] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[802] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m```bash[39m                                                           [0m]8;;
[803] (w=67)    tmux set-option -p -t [38;2;158;206;106m"[38;2;255;158;100m$TMUX_PANE[39m"[39m @agent pi                    [0m]8;;
[804] (w=67)    [38;2;125;207;255mexec[39m pi                                                         [0m]8;;
[805] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m```[39m                                                               [0m]8;;
[806] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[807] (w=67)  Then search for [38;2;158;206;106m@agent[39m instead of [38;2;158;206;106mpane_current_command[39m.           [0m]8;;
[808] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[809] (w=67)  [38;2;255;158;100m[1m### [22m[39m[38;2;255;158;100m[1mOption 2: fallback to text matching[22m[39m                           [0m]8;;
[810] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[811] (w=67)  Use [38;2;158;206;106mcapture-pane[39m and inspect visible text for clues like:         [0m]8;;
[812] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[813] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[38;2;158;206;106mWorking...[39m                                                      [0m]8;;
[814] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[38;2;158;206;106mclaude[39m                                                          [0m]8;;
[815] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[38;2;158;206;106mcodex[39m                                                           [0m]8;;
[816] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39mapproval prompts                                                [0m]8;;
[817] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[818] (w=67)  That’s more brittle, but possible later.                          [0m]8;;
[819] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[820] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[39m [0m]8;;
[821] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[822] (w=67)  [38;2;255;158;100m[1mBest path for your use case[22m[39m                                       [0m]8;;
[823] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[824] (w=67)  For [1mv1[22m, I’d do this:                                              [0m]8;;
[825] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[826] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39mtry [38;2;158;206;106mpane_current_command[39m first                                  [0m]8;;
[827] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39mif that’s unreliable for your agents, switch to explicit pane   [0m]8;;
[828] (w=67)  tagging via wrappers                                              [0m]8;;
[829] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[830] (w=67)  That will get you the search/jump feature quickly.                [0m]8;;
[831] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[832] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[39m [0m]8;;
[833] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[834] (w=67)  [38;2;255;158;100m[1mAbout state later[22m[39m                                                 [0m]8;;
[835] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[836] (w=67)  Also possible, just not needed for v1.                            [0m]8;;
[837] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[838] (w=67)  You could store:                                                  [0m]8;;
[839] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[840] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[38;2;158;206;106m@agent=pi[39m                                                       [0m]8;;
[841] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[38;2;158;206;106m@agent_state=working|blocked|idle[39m                               [0m]8;;
[842] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[843] (w=67)  and then show it in the fzf list.                                 [0m]8;;
[844] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[845] (w=67)  But your main feature — [1msearch agent panes and jump to them[22m — is  [0m]8;;
[846] (w=67)  definitely doable right now.                                      [0m]8;;
[847] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[848] (w=67)  If you want, I can write a slightly more robust version that:     [0m]8;;
[849] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39mdetects by both [38;2;158;206;106mpane_current_command[39m [1mand[22m [38;2;158;206;106m@agent[39m                 [0m]8;;
[850] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39mshows nice labels in [38;2;158;206;106mfzf[39m                                        [0m]8;;
[851] (w=67) ]133;B]133;C [38;2;125;207;255m- [39mfits into your existing [38;2;158;206;106mtms[39m flow as [38;2;158;206;106mtms agents[39m                  [0m]8;;
