[858] (w=67)  [1m[3m[38;2;86;95;137mExplaining tmux pane naming[39m[23m[22m                                       [0m]8;;
[859] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[860] (w=67)  [3m[38;2;86;95;137mI need to focus on how naming works in tmux, especially since     [0m]8;;
[861] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137mpanes don’t have built-in names and there can be multiple agents  [0m]8;;
[862] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137min one window. I should propose a practical labeling scheme for   [0m]8;;
[863] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137msearch results. In tmux, panes have attributes like pane_title    [0m]8;;
[864] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137mand pane_index, while windows have names. [39m[23m                        [0m]8;;
[865] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[866] (w=67)  [3m[38;2;86;95;137mWe could create a custom pane-local label option and derive it    [0m]8;;
[867] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137mfrom window_name, pane_index, current working directory, and the  [0m]8;;
[868] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137mcurrent command. This way, search results could look like         [0m]8;;
[869] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137msession:window.pane, helping to distinguish between multiple      [0m]8;;
[870] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137magents in a window.[39m[23m                                               [0m]8;;
[871] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[872] (w=67)  [1m[3m[38;2;86;95;137mExplaining label options[39m[23m[22m                                          [0m]8;;
[873] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[874] (w=67)  [3m[38;2;86;95;137mI need to clarify the different labeling options available for    [0m]8;;
[875] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137mpanes. First, there’s the location tuple format, which looks like [0m]8;;
[876] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137msession:window.pane. Then, we can derive labels from either the   [0m]8;;
[877] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137mcurrent working directory's basename or the basename of the git   [0m]8;;
[878] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137mrepository. [39m[23m                                                      [0m]8;;
[879] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[880] (w=67)  [3m[38;2;86;95;137mI should also include the option for a custom label stored in     [0m]8;;
[881] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137m@pane_label or @agent_label. To provide a comprehensive answer,   [0m]8;;
[882] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137mI’ll propose some formats and a recommended approach for crafting [0m]8;;
[883] (w=67)  [3;38;2;86;95;137mconcise yet useful labels.[39m[23m                                        [0m]8;;
[884] (w=0) [0m]8;;
[885] (w=67)  Yeah — I wouldn’t treat this as “panes need names.”               [0m]8;;
[886] (w=67)  For tmux, the better model is:                                    [0m]8;;
[887] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[888] (w=67)  [38;2;255;158;100m[1mPanes don’t need names, they need a good [22m[39m[1m[38;2;255;158;100m[1mlabel[22m[1m[39m[22m                    [0m]8;;
[889] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[890] (w=67)  A search result can be identified by a combination of:            [0m]8;;
[891] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[892] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[1msession name[22m                                                    [0m]8;;
[893] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[1mwindow name/index[22m                                               [0m]8;;
[894] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[1mpane index/id[22m                                                   [0m]8;;
[895] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[1mcurrent path[22m or repo name                                       [0m]8;;
[896] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[1magent type[22m ([38;2;158;206;106mpi[39m, [38;2;158;206;106mcodex[39m, etc.)                                    [0m]8;;
[897] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39mmaybe a [1mpreview[22m of recent pane output                           [0m]8;;
[898] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[899] (w=67)  That’s enough to make panes searchable and distinguish multiple   [0m]8;;
[900] (w=67)  agents in the same window.                                        [0m]8;;
[901] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[902] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[39m [0m]8;;
[903] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[904] (w=67)  [38;2;255;158;100m[1mGood default identity[22m[39m                                             [0m]8;;
[905] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[906] (w=67)  In tmux, every pane already has a stable locator like:            [0m]8;;
[907] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[908] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m```text[39m                                                           [0m]8;;
[909] (w=67)    session:window.pane                                             [0m]8;;
[910] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m```[39m                                                               [0m]8;;
[911] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[912] (w=67)  Example:                                                          [0m]8;;
[913] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[914] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m```text[39m                                                           [0m]8;;
[915] (w=67)    work:3.1                                                        [0m]8;;
[916] (w=67)    work:3.2                                                        [0m]8;;
[917] (w=67)    side:1.0                                                        [0m]8;;
[918] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m```[39m                                                               [0m]8;;
[919] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[920] (w=67)  So if you have multiple agents in one window, that’s fine:        [0m]8;;
[921] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[922] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[38;2;158;206;106mwork:3.1[39m = pi in repo A                                         [0m]8;;
[923] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[38;2;158;206;106mwork:3.2[39m = codex in repo B                                      [0m]8;;
[924] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[925] (w=67)  The “name” can just be a display label built from metadata.       [0m]8;;
[926] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[927] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[39m [0m]8;;
[928] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[929] (w=67)  [38;2;255;158;100m[1mRecommended v1 display format[22m[39m                                     [0m]8;;
[930] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[931] (w=67)  I’d show something like this in [38;2;158;206;106mfzf[39m:                              [0m]8;;
[932] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[933] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m```text[39m                                                           [0m]8;;
[934] (w=67)    work:3.1  pi     herdr        /Users/josh/project/herdr         [0m]8;;
[935] (w=67)    work:3.2  codex  website      /Users/josh/project/herdr/website [0m]8;;
[936] (w=67)    ops:1.0   claude infra        /Users/josh/infra                 [0m]8;;
[937] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m```[39m                                                               [0m]8;;
[938] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[939] (w=67)  Where columns are:                                                [0m]8;;
[940] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[941] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m1. [39m[1mpane locator[22m: [38;2;158;206;106msession:window.pane[39m                              [0m]8;;
[942] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m2. [39m[1magent[22m: [38;2;158;206;106mpi[39m, [38;2;158;206;106mclaude[39m, etc.                                        [0m]8;;
[943] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m3. [39m[1mderived short label[22m: maybe basename of cwd / repo              [0m]8;;
[944] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m4. [39m[1mfull path[22m                                                      [0m]8;;
[945] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[946] (w=67)  That already solves most of the ambiguity.                        [0m]8;;
[947] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[948] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[39m [0m]8;;
[949] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[950] (w=67)  [38;2;255;158;100m[1mWhere the label should come from[22m[39m                                  [0m]8;;
[951] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[952] (w=67)  [38;2;255;158;100m[1m### [22m[39m[38;2;255;158;100m[1mOption 1: current path basename[22m[39m                               [0m]8;;
[953] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[954] (w=67)  Probably the best default.                                        [0m]8;;
[955] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[956] (w=67)  Examples:                                                         [0m]8;;
[957] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[38;2;158;206;106m/Users/josh/work/herdr[39m → [38;2;158;206;106mherdr[39m                                  [0m]8;;
[958] (w=67)  [38;2;125;207;255m- [39m[38;2;158;206;106m/Users/josh/work/dotfiles[39m → [38;2;158;206;106mdotfiles[39m                            [0m]8;;
[959] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[960] (w=67)  This is nice because agents are often tied to a repo.             [0m]8;;
[961] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[962] (w=67)  [38;2;255;158;100m[1m### [22m[39m[38;2;255;158;100m[1mOption 2: window name + pane index[22m[39m                            [0m]8;;
[963] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[964] (w=67)  If your windows are already named well, use:                      [0m]8;;
[965] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[966] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m```text[39m                                                           [0m]8;;
[967] (w=67)    work/api#1                                                      [0m]8;;
[968] (w=67)    work/api#2                                                      [0m]8;;
[969] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m```[39m                                                               [0m]8;;
[970] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[971] (w=67)  [38;2;255;158;100m[1m### [22m[39m[38;2;255;158;100m[1mOption 3: custom pane label[22m[39m                                   [0m]8;;
[972] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[973] (w=67)  If you want better names later, store your own pane-local option: [0m]8;;
[974] (w=67)                                                                    [0m]8;;
[975] (w=67)  [38;2;59;66;97m```bash[39m                                                           [0m]8;;
